(B3 class B: a notation wrapper over `pd`, bridge `pdM_apply` is `rfl`). `SmoothOn A U` says every entry
is `C^∞` on `U`. On an open set all the usual rules hold with genuine derivatives:

* product rule `pdM i (A·B) = (pdM i A)·B + A·(pdM i B)`, linearity, finite sums, scalar multiples;
* derivative of an inverse: `K·J = 1` on `U` ⇒ `pdM i K = −K·(pdM i J)·K`;
* chain rule `pdM i (B ∘ Φ) y = Σ_e J y e i • pdM e B (Φ y)`;
* symmetry `pdM c (pdM d A) = pdM d (pdM c A)`;
* smoothness of a right inverse `K` of a smooth `J` (`K = det(J)⁻¹ • adjugate J`), and of the genuine
